          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On October 9, 2018, around 9 PM, two people in the same vehicle were driving on highway A11 between ANCENIS (44) and NANTES (44). Suddenly, their attention was drawn by one or two very bright lights moving from left to right in the clear sky. The observation was very brief (a few seconds). The witnesses are unsure of what they saw. The case consistency is fairly good (see the investigation report): - Two direct, non-independent witnesses (friends), - An incomplete subjective reconstruction (unclear time and location), - No additional technical elements (photos or videos). The strangeness is relatively low with only one hypothesis considered. The general description of the PAN strongly suggests a meteor, given its luminous aspect, its very high apparent speed, and its very short observation duration, but no meteor could be linked to the observation, despite the various dedicated surveillance networks currently in place. Therefore, the hypothesis is probable but not certain. The GEIPAN classifies this case as B: probable observation of a meteor.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "8341cfd49e6d01a697cb0a90f84c8a8d252a505fc90cef1766bf1b2bb1d3d3e7"
        }
